          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+geometry"} prequantum geometry
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            which are equipped with a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twist
            in the form of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            and a circle-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"}> principal connection
            \. In the context of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            these arise as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+bundles"} prequantum bundles
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contact+geometry"} contact geometry
            of the total spaces of these bundles, equipped with their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connection"} Ehresmann connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-form"} differential 1-form
            and thought of as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+contact+manifolds"} regular contact manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+bundles"} prequantum bundles
            covering
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            of the base – the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+operators"} prequantum operators
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contactomorphisms"} contactomorphisms
            – and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of these on the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            – the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+states"} prequantum states
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-form"} differential 2-form
            of these bundles, which is obtained by “dividing the above data in half” (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"}> polarization
            ), important for instance in the the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
          %p
            But prequantum geometry is of interest in its own right. For instance the above automorphism group naturally provides the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of the underlying
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+bisections"} group of bisections
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+algebroid"} Atiyah Lie algebroid
            which is associated with the given circle bundle, all of which are fundamental objects of interest in the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundles"} line bundles
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
          %p
            For a plethora of applications in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+higher+differential+geometry"} motivation for higher differential geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %em higher prequantum geometry
          %h2#motivation_and_survey_of_results Motivation and survey of results
          %h3#OrdinaryPrequantumGeometryInTermsofAutomorphismsInSlices Ordinary prequantum geometry in terms of automorphisms in slices
          %p
            A sequence of time-honored traditional concepts in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+geometry"} prequantum geometry
            is
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"}> Lie groups
                  \:
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ↪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ↪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"}> Lie algebras
                  \:
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ↪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebra"} Poisson Lie algebra
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ↪
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  twisted
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+fields"} vector fields
          %p
            For instance in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electrically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+particle"} charged
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle"} particle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+bundle"} prequantum circle bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = T^* Y
            which is essentially the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of the
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
            is the group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} P
            of the total space of the prequantum bundle which preserve the connection (also called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contactomorphism"} contactomorphism
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (P,\nabla)
            regarded as a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+contact+manifold"} regular contact manifold
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            (a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"}> smooth space
            ”) and then moreover as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            on this site (a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"}> smooth groupoid
            ”) and make use of the tautological existence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
            (we don’t need further details right now, but they can be found for instance at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
            for details). By definition this is such that for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \colon X \to \mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
            is equivalently a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            and such that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon \nabla_1 \to \nabla_2
            between two such maps is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            between two such connections. With this formulation a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism"} quantomorphism
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+bundle"} prequantum bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            is equivalently a diagram of the form as on the right of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi QuantMorph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↙
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi conn
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{QuantMorph}(\nabla)
                  \=
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;&amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{\phi}{\to}&amp;&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;\swArrow_{\eta}&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
                  }
                  \\right\}
          %p
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} X
            of the base space of the bundle together with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∇
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon \phi^* \nabla \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \nabla
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
            is naturally an (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+Lie+group"}> infinite dimensional
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            itself (notably if it is a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+differential+form"} invariant vectors
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
            and the Lie group corresponding to that is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
          %p
            One also says that a triangular diagram as above is an autoequivalence of the “modulating” map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
